{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban the killing of day-old male chicks and require in-ovo sexing",
        "additional_details": "Male chicks from egg-laying breeds may be killed shortly after hatching because they cannot lay eggs. In-ovo sexing can determine their sex before hatching\r\nand is already used commercially in countries including\r\n\r\nGermany and France. Germany and France have also introduced bans on the routine killing of male chicks. We believe the UK Government should require in-ovo sexing to prevent the avoidable killing of newly hatched male chicks.\r\n",
        "background": "Require the UK Government to prohibit the routine killing of healthy day-old male chicks in the egg industry and require hatcheries to use in-ovo sexing\r\ntechnology to identify male embryos before hatching.\r\n",
